  "worked_solution": "We can find the necessary function values using the graph.\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- When $x=-3,$ the function is undefined.\n\n- When $x=3,$ we have $y=-2.$ So, $f(3)=-2.$\n\nTherefore, since $f(-3)$ is undefined, the sum $f(-3)+f(3)$ is undefined too.",
